🛒 E-Commerce Customer Segmentation & Product Performance Analytics
Project Overview
This project analyzes a transactional e-commerce dataset to evaluate product revenue performance, regional sales trends, and customer value distribution. By combining Python-based exploratory data analysis (EDA) and machine learning with an interactive Power BI dashboard, this project transforms raw transaction logs into actionable commercial insights.

The workflow bridges the gap between product-level performance tracking and behavioral customer segmentation (RFM & K-Means Clustering) to help businesses identify top revenue drivers and protect high-value customer cohorts.

Built Using
Python — Data cleaning, feature engineering, statistical analysis, and machine learning clustering

Pandas & NumPy — Data manipulation, aggregation, and array transformations

Scikit-Learn — Unsupervised machine learning (K-Means Clustering for RFM segmentation)

Matplotlib & Seaborn — Advanced data visualization and trend plotting

Power BI — Interactive executive dashboarding and stakeholder reporting

Dataset Overview
The dataset consists of detailed international e-commerce transaction records containing information about invoice numbers, stock codes, product descriptions, quantities, invoice dates, unit prices, customer IDs, and country regions.

Data preparation involved:

Handling missing values and filtering out cancelled or anomalous transactions (e.g., negative quantities/returns).

Converting date fields and engineering aggregate metrics (Recency, Frequency, Monetary values per customer).

Creating calculated fields for total revenue and estimated profit proxies.

Exploratory Data Analysis & Business Insights
Python was utilized to investigate core commercial questions before building the clustering model and dashboard:

1. Product Revenue & Profitability Analysis
Top Revenue Drivers: Grouping transactions by product description revealed a heavy reliance on standout best-sellers, led by the Regency Cakestand 3 Tier (£174K+ in total revenue).

Profit Proxy: Due to the absence of explicit cost-of-goods-sold (COGS) data, an industry-standard 30% gross margin benchmark was modeled to estimate product profitability and highlight high-return inventory items.

2. Regional & Monthly Trend Diagnostics
Core Market Dominance: Time-series aggregation across 38 international regions proved that the United Kingdom accounts for the vast majority of transaction volume and revenue.

Seasonal Peak Analysis: The UK market displayed massive Q4 holiday momentum, peaking dramatically in November before a sharp drop in December (identified as a data collection truncation artifact rather than business churn).

3. Customer Value Segmentation (RFM + K-Means)
Customers were segmented based on their purchasing behavior:

Champions: High spenders with recent and frequent visits.

Core Regulars: Steady, reliable buyers forming the baseline of daily volume.

At-Risk / Lost: Dormant customers requiring re-engagement strategies.

Power BI Dashboard Structure
The Power BI dashboard translates the analytical findings into a clean, executive-ready interface featuring dynamic interactivity:

Page 1: Customer Volume & Segment Distribution

Clustered column charts tracking customer counts across Champions, Core Regulars, and At-Risk/Lost tiers.

Page 2: Financial Impact & Revenue Contribution

Revenue breakdown charts highlighting exactly which segment drives the highest monetary returns.

Page 3: Recency vs. Monetary Scatter Plot

An interactive customer-level scatter plot color-coded by cluster segments to visually map customer lifetime value against activity recency.

Interactive Navigation:

Modern tile slicers enabling stakeholders to instantly filter the entire canvas by specific customer segments.

Skills & Capabilities Demonstrated
Advanced Data Cleaning & Wrangling (Pandas)

Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) & Time-Series Trend Breakdown

Unsupervised Machine Learning (K-Means Clustering & RFM Modeling)

Feature Engineering & Proxy Metric Modeling (Estimated Profit Benchmarks)

Data Visualization (Matplotlib, Seaborn, Power BI)

Executive Dashboard Development & Slicer Interactivity

Business Insight Generation & Strategic Storytelling

Project Objective
The primary objective of this project is to demonstrate how raw transactional data can be systematically cleaned, modeled, and visualized to answer critical business questions: Who are our most valuable customers, which products drive our top-line growth, and how do regional sales trends evolve over time?
